From b86ec901c5c965e349ae1d96ceef0ad2f06f6414 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:50:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] vu1: leaner scheduled blocks and lazy flag commits

- Blocks are split at branch targets and may end in a branch and its delay
  slot; they run only while PATH1 is idle, so pairs inside need no PATH1 or
  stop checks (one m_blockOff flag), and advance with ++m_cycle.
- VF0/VI0 are reset only after pairs that can write register 0 (decoder
  flag writesReg0); register save/restore around exec only where needed;
  the branch-read backup only where a branch can read it.
- MAC/status/clip results are committed when read (the flag-reading lower
  instructions, FDIV status commit, a full ring, run end, flush) instead of
  every cycle; queueStore is inline; the write-only current-upper field is
  gone.
- GA2_VU1_BLOCKSTATS=1 (ga2_vu1_check) prints block entry/guard statistics.

Callgrind (generated path): narration 823.8M -> 592.5M Ir, map 754.3M ->
543.6M. ga2_vu1_check --reference: 0 mismatches on narration, map, battle,
tutorial; random-program fuzzing against the previous interpreter (4.5M
programs) and block steps (6M trials): 0 mismatches. ps2x_tests 579/579.
In game: Zettai battle 21:9, Mugen 1 tutorial battle, Eigou 2 narration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
